+- **`demand-tools-sync` runs the two Demand Tools writes at 4am America/Denver.**
+  Vercel cron is UTC only, so the route is scheduled at 10:00 and 11:00 UTC and
+  answers `{ ok: true, skipped: true }` unless the Denver hour is 4
+  (`isNightlyWindow`). Exactly one of the two fires each day, in MDT and in MST.
+  Both steps read prices and item fields from BigQuery `items.items_netsuite`
+  (`fetchItemEnrichment`), not from the Postgres mirror that
+  `netsuite-items-reconcile` refreshes at 08:15 UTC, so the run is only as
+  fresh as whatever feeds that table. A step requests a mirror push only for the
+  months it changed, so a night with no price or division change queues nothing.
+  The 15:00 UTC `plan-push-full` rebuild still repairs any miss the same day.
+  The 06:00 to 07:15 UTC snapshots (`eom-snapshot`, `inventory-report-snapshot`,
+  `demand-plan-snapshot`, `wholesale-comp-snapshot`) run before this job, so a
+  price change shows in them the next day. The steps run one after another, item
+  fields first, because both rewrite `supply_plan_monthly` for the same pairs. A step
+  that fails alerts, the other step still runs, and the route answers 500. The
+  reprice covers every month, same as the button, and keeps each row's own plan
+  discount (ADR 0004). A UPC with no base price is skipped, never zeroed.
+
 ### Snapshots and checks
 
 - **`eom-snapshot` runs the same write as the toolbar Export EOM button**
